      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "Write the first four nonzero terms of the Maclaurin series for \\( h \\). Then find the value of \\( h^{(5)}(0) \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "h: \\; x - x^{2} + \\frac{2}{3}x^{3} - \\frac{1}{3}x^{4}, \\qquad h^{(5)}(0) = 16",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Integrate the series for f term by term from 0 to x.",
               "latex": "h(x) = \\int_{0}^{x} \\left(1 - 2t + 2t^{2} - \\frac{4}{3}t^{3} + \\frac{2}{3}t^{4} - \\cdots\\right) dt"
            },
            {
               "text": "The first four nonzero terms.",
               "latex": "h(x) \\approx x - x^{2} + \\frac{2}{3}x^{3} - \\frac{1}{3}x^{4}"
            },
            {
               "text": "The x^5 coefficient of h is (2/3)/5 = 2/15, so h^(5)(0) = 5! times 2/15, which also equals f^(4)(0).",
               "latex": "h^{(5)}(0) = 120 \\cdot \\frac{2}{15} = 16"
            }
         ],
